Description: Increase sleep time in a treading test
 In Debian CI fails a test that use sleep(0.05) and in some machine apparently
 they don't have enough time to finished. Thanks cjwatson to noted it.
Author: Emmanuel Arias
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2025-03-19
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/tests/utils/test_threading.py
+++ b/tests/utils/test_threading.py
@@ -42,7 +42,7 @@
 
     def _compute_value(self) -> int:
         # we block the thread here to ensure contention
-        time.sleep(0.05)
+        time.sleep(5)
         return self.compute_value(self._name, time.time())
 
     @functools.cached_property
